From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu2023@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] port/dwc2: serve full-speed isochronous urbs one packet at a time

The DWC2 host port had no isochronous submit path: usbh_submit_urb() left
the iso case empty and the channel-halt interrupt had an empty iso branch, so
a UVC camera's streaming endpoint was never serviced.  This adds the engine
the full-speed UVC image needs.

The core reports only the total length of the transaction it halted, but UVC
needs every payload packet's length to parse its variable-length payload
header.  The engine therefore programs one iso_packet[] entry per channel
activation (PKTCNT=1), records its actual_length from HCTSIZ's remaining
size, and re-arms the same channel for the next entry from the halt interrupt.
This is the per-frame model Linux's dwc2 host driver uses for iso urbs.

One channel per endpoint is the contract: a second in-flight urb for the same
endpoint is refused with -USB_ERR_BUSY.  The UVC stream engine is configured
for a single urb and resubmits it after the pump has consumed it; the
synchronous path (timeout > 0) is used by the ISO smoke case.  Per-packet
errors are recorded on the iso_packet entry and do not kill the urb; a halt
without XFRC costs exactly one packet.  The engine implements IN only (the UVC
streaming direction).

The code is compiled only under CONFIG_USB_DWC2_ISO, which the UVC cases
select in platform/build_defs.h; every other F429 USB image keeps the port's
pin bytes and pays no code size.

diff --git a/third-party/cherryusb/port/dwc2/usb_hc_dwc2.c b/third-party/cherryusb/port/dwc2/usb_hc_dwc2.c
